messages[13]{user,text}:
  user_1,[00:00] Hello? Hi, um... this is Sneha Roy, calling about my auto policy.
  user_2,[00:05] Hi Sneha, Anjali speaking from First Guard Brokers. How can I help you today?
  user_1,[00:12] Yeah, I got the quote you sent—₹11,828 after discount. I was just wondering—uh—what happens if I don’t pay today?
  user_2,[00:20] ...If the payment isn’t received by the due date, the policy will stay in a lapsed state and technically be expired as of 15 August 2026.
  user_1,[00:28] Oh, I see. I was actually thinking maybe I’ll hold off for a bit—
  user_2,--? Sorry, could you repeat that?
  user_1,[00:35] I said, I might not renew right now. I’m not sure I need the coverage at the moment.
  user_2,[00:40] I understand. Just to confirm, you’d like us to close the policy and let it remain expired?
  user_1,[00:45] Yes, that’s correct. I don’t want any further charges.
  user_2,[00:50] Alright, I’ll mark it as expired in our system. You’ll receive a confirmation email shortly.
  user_1,[00:55] Thanks, Anjali. Sorry for the back‑and‑forth.
  user_2,[01:00] No problem at all, Sneha. If you ever need coverage again, just give us a call. Have a good day.
  user_1,[01:05] You too, bye.